# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/expansion_life.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event life_timeloop_1
# en: Haven't We Done This?
title [f7db95] = 这事是不是发生过？
# en: Breakfast. Eggs. Thorne trips on the third step. A first-year spills juice on a prefect. You know all of this is about to happen, because it already happened. Yesterday. Which was also Tuesday.
text [8f145a] = 早餐。鸡蛋。索恩在第三级台阶上绊了一下。一个一年级生把果汁洒在了级长身上。你知道这一切马上就要发生，因为它已经发生过了。昨天。昨天也是星期二。
# en: A student at breakfast staring at a plate of eggs with intense déjà vu, a clock on the wall with its hands spinning backward.
scene [f64ed4] = 一名学生在早餐桌前盯着一盘鸡蛋，强烈的既视感涌上心头，墙上的钟指针在倒转。
# en: Ignore it — probably just tired
opt.left.label [d0cdc9] = 不管了——大概只是累了
# en: You eat the eggs. They taste exactly as they did yesterday. Thorne trips on the third step.
opt.left.say.1 [e481ca] = 你吃了鸡蛋。味道和昨天一模一样。索恩在第三级台阶上绊了一下。
# en: Warn Thorne about the step
opt.right.label [eb6211] = 提醒索恩小心台阶
# en: "The third step, Professor." He looks at you strangely and steps over it. Somewhere, a clock skips. It's still Tuesday.
opt.right.say.1 [8ba6ad] = “第三级台阶，教授。”他奇怪地看了你一眼，跨了过去。某处，一座钟跳了一格。还是星期二。

@event life_timeloop_2
# en: Tuesday, Again
title [d04f00] = 又是星期二
# en: It's Tuesday. Again. For the fourth time. Nobody else notices. On the bright side, you now know every answer in this afternoon's quiz. On the dark side, it's Tuesday. Forever.
text [b8ccb9] = 星期二。又是。第四次了。没有别人注意到。往好处想，你现在知道今天下午小测的每一道答案。往坏处想，今天是星期二。永远是。
# en: The same breakfast scene repeated, but the student is now standing on the table, holding up a sign that reads "IT'S STILL TUESDAY".
scene [443eec] = 同样的早餐场景再次上演，但这一次学生站在了桌子上，举着一块牌子：“现在还是星期二”。
# en: Use it — ace the quiz, win every bet
opt.left.label [c29420] = 利用它——考满分，赌必赢
# en: You win every bet, ace the quiz, and catch the juice before it hits the prefect. On the sixth Tuesday it starts to feel hollow. Something has to give.
opt.left.say.1 [fbd1e9] = 你赢了每一场赌局，小测拿了满分，还在果汁泼到级长之前接住了它。到第六个星期二，这一切开始变得空洞。总得有什么东西松动才行。
# en: Find the cause
opt.right.label [12f556] = 找出原因
# en: You spend three Tuesdays in the library. On the fourth you find it: someone in the astronomy tower has wound an old chronometer backward. With a wand.
opt.right.say.1 [8ee226] = 你在图书馆里度过了三个星期二。第四个星期二，你找到了：天文塔里有人用魔杖把一台古老的计时仪倒着上了发条。

@event life_timeloop_3
# en: The Broken Chronometer
title [d82d49] = 坏掉的计时仪
# en: In the astronomy tower, a first-year is asleep beside an enormous brass chronometer, wand still stuck in its winding key. "I just wanted one more day before my exam," says the note on his chest.
text [94f829] = 天文塔里，一个一年级生睡在一台巨大的黄铜计时仪旁边，魔杖还卡在发条钥匙里。他胸前的字条上写着：“我只是想在考试前多要一天。”
# en: An astronomy tower at night, a giant brass chronometer with its gears spinning in reverse, a sleeping first-year slumped beside it with a wand still in hand.
scene [4ad62e] = 夜晚的天文塔，一台巨型黄铜计时仪的齿轮在倒转，一个睡着的一年级生瘫在旁边，手里还握着魔杖。
# en: Fix the chronometer (Arcana)
opt.left.label [d9f43c] = 修好计时仪（奥术）
# en: You ease the wand out and the gears groan forward. Wednesday arrives like a sneeze. Nobody but you and one mortified first-year ever knows.
opt.left.say.1 [a7de56] = 你轻轻抽出魔杖，齿轮吱嘎着向前转动。星期三像一个喷嚏一样到来了。除了你和一个羞愧万分的一年级生，没人知道这件事。
# en: The chronometer bites. It takes you two more Tuesdays and a lot of swearing. But eventually, gloriously, it's Wednesday.
opt.left.say.2 [276d7c] = 计时仪咬人。你又花了两个星期二、骂了不少脏话。但最终，光荣地，星期三来了。
# en: Teach the first-year to fix it
opt.right.label [eb58e0] = 教那个一年级生自己修
# en: You show him how. He fixes his own mess, cries a little, and promises never to touch a clock again. Wednesday arrives. He passes his exam.
opt.right.say.1 [c72a99] = 你教他怎么做。他亲手收拾了自己的烂摊子，哭了一小会儿，发誓再也不碰钟了。星期三来了。他考试及格了。

@event life_portrait_escape
# en: The Escaped Portrait
title [2a676c] = 出逃的画像
# en: An empty frame in the long gallery. The Duchess of Ambry has escaped her portrait and is hiding in a landscape three corridors away, refusing to come back. "That frame," she declares, "is hideous."
text [a18812] = 长廊里一个空画框。安布里公爵夫人逃出了她的画像，躲进了三条走廊外的一幅风景画里，拒绝回来。“那个画框，”她宣布，“丑死了。”
# en: An empty gilded picture frame on a gallery wall, and further down the corridor a painted duchess hiding inside a landscape of a picnic.
scene [805579] = 长廊墙上一个空空的镀金画框，走廊尽头，一位画中的公爵夫人正躲在一幅野餐风景画里。
# en: Persuade her back (Charm)
opt.left.label [ad9688] = 劝她回来（魅力）
# en: You promise to have her frame regilded. She returns, mollified. The caretaker regilds it. You've acquired a duchess who now considers you a personal friend.
opt.left.say.1 [af9e67] = 你答应给她的画框重新镀金。她回来了，气消了。管理员重新镀了金。你收获了一位公爵夫人，她现在把你当作私人朋友。
# en: She calls you a peasant and moves to a painting of a shipwreck. She's still there. She says she likes the sea air.
opt.left.say.2 [7c07eb] = 她骂你是个乡巴佬，搬进了一幅沉船图里。她至今还在那儿。她说她喜欢海风。
# en: Leave her in the picnic
opt.right.label [f13545] = 让她留在野餐里
# en: She seems happier among the sandwiches. So does the picnic. Some arrangements simply work.
opt.right.say.1 [09beab] = 她在三明治之间似乎更快乐。野餐也是。有些安排就是刚刚好。

@event life_library_cat
# en: The Library Cat
title [d3cfff] = 图书馆的猫
# en: The library cat — a vast, ancient beast called Footnote — is asleep on the only copy of the book you need. You have an essay due tomorrow. Footnote has no deadlines.
text [968aad] = 图书馆的猫——一只名叫“脚注”的巨大古老生物——正睡在你需要的那本书上，而那是唯一的一本。你的论文明天就要交。脚注没有截止日期。
# en: An enormous fluffy cat asleep on the exact book a student needs, on a high library shelf, one eye half-open.
scene [8ac48f] = 一只巨大的蓬松猫咪睡在图书馆高处书架上，身下正是学生需要的那本书，一只眼睛半睁着。
# en: Move the cat (Vigor)
opt.left.label [6b98b1] = 把猫挪开（体魄）
# en: You lift Footnote like a sack of warm flour. He allows it, with contempt. You get the book. He gets your chair.
opt.left.say.1 [52e940] = 你像抱一袋温热的面粉一样抱起脚注。它允许了，带着鄙夷。你拿到了书。它拿到了你的椅子。
# en: Footnote does not consent to being moved. You now have three long scratches and still no book.
opt.left.say.2 [6230a8] = 脚注不同意被挪动。你现在多了三道长长的抓痕，书还是没拿到。
# en: Bribe the cat
opt.right.label [011f22] = 贿赂这只猫
# en: One sardine. Footnote rises like a sultan, stretches, and moves exactly one book to the left. It's enough.
opt.right.say.1 [b290a1] = 一条沙丁鱼。脚注像苏丹一样起身，伸了个懒腰，正好往左挪了一本书的距离。够了。

@event life_invent_spell
# en: A Spell of Your Own
title [9d35aa] = 属于你的咒语
# en: Late at night you realise there's a gap — a spell nobody has written yet, just a small one, to make ink dry instantly. You could try to invent it. Inventing spells, Thorne says, is "how most of my former students lost their eyebrows".
text [40816d] = 深夜，你意识到有个空白——一个还没人写过的咒语，只是个小咒语，能让墨水瞬间变干。你可以试着发明它。索恩说，发明咒语是“我大多数前学生失去眉毛的方式”。
# en: A student at a desk covered in crossed-out incantations, a tiny spiral of light hovering over the page, an expression of dawning triumph.
scene [c075ca] = 一名学生坐在写满划掉的咒文的书桌前，一小团螺旋状的光悬浮在纸上，脸上渐渐露出胜利的神情。
# en: Invent it carefully (Lore)
opt.left.label [b36170] = 小心地发明它（学识）
# en: Three weeks of theory and one perfect evening. The spell works. Thorne grunts and puts your name on the lecture slide for next year. Forever.
opt.left.say.1 [5b2d62] = 三个星期的理论，加上一个完美的夜晚。咒语成功了。索恩哼了一声，把你的名字放上了明年的讲义。永远。
# en: Your spell dries ink instantly. It also dries the paper, the desk and your eyes. You shelve it for now.
opt.left.say.2 [20cce9] = 你的咒语能瞬间弄干墨水。也能弄干纸、书桌和你的眼睛。你暂时把它搁置了。
# en: Just try things until something works
opt.right.label [847e81] = 乱试一通，直到有效
# en: Somehow — through chaos and luck — it works. You couldn't explain why under oath. It still counts.
opt.right.say.1 [c2baba] = 不知怎么的——靠着混乱和运气——它成功了。就算发誓你也解释不了为什么。但它照样算数。
# en: Your eyebrows survive. Your desk does not.
opt.right.say.2 [182ef8] = 你的眉毛幸存了。你的书桌没有。

@event life_cursed_umbrella
# en: The Cursed Umbrella
title [8c3b3e] = 被诅咒的伞
# en: You borrowed an umbrella from lost property. It's black, elegant and cursed: underneath it, it is always raining. The rest of the world is sunny. You are very wet.
text [b42225] = 你从失物招领处借了一把伞。它是黑色的，很优雅，还被诅咒了：伞底下永远在下雨。外面整个世界阳光明媚。你浑身湿透。
# en: A student holding a black umbrella under which a tiny private rainstorm is pouring, while the sky outside is perfectly clear.
scene [3ed21b] = 一名学生撑着一把黑伞，伞下正下着一场私人小暴雨，而外面的天空晴朗无云。
# en: Break the curse (Arcana)
opt.left.label [553d6a] = 解除诅咒（奥术）
# en: The curse lifts with a soft hiss. The umbrella is now just a very nice umbrella. You sell it to Corvin, who wants it "for drama".
opt.left.say.1 [037847] = 诅咒轻轻嘶的一声解除了。现在它只是一把非常好看的伞。你把它卖给了科尔文，他说要拿来“营造戏剧效果”。
# en: Now it rains sideways.
opt.left.say.2 [1a72a4] = 现在雨是横着下的。
# en: Return it to lost property
opt.right.label [5ea06a] = 还给失物招领处
# en: The caretaker takes it back, sighs, and hangs it on a hook labelled "DO NOT". There are six other things on that hook.
opt.right.say.1 [c90b55] = 管理员收了回去，叹了口气，把它挂在一个标着“别碰”的钩子上。那个钩子上已经挂了六样别的东西。

@event life_exam_dream
# en: The Exam Dream
title [e7738c] = 考试噩梦
# en: You dream you're in the exam hall in your pyjamas. The paper is in a language that keeps changing. The proctor is Bartholomew the goat. You wake at 4am, heart pounding.
text [4ad83e] = 你梦见自己穿着睡衣坐在考场里。试卷上的语言不停地变来变去。监考官是山羊巴塞洛缪。凌晨四点你惊醒了，心怦怦直跳。
# en: A dream-image: a student in an exam hall in their pyjamas, the exam paper written in a language that keeps changing, a clock with no hands.
scene [e45f4e] = 梦境画面：一名学生穿着睡衣坐在考场里，试卷上的文字不停变换，一座没有指针的钟。
# en: Get up and revise
opt.left.label [02956b] = 起床复习
# en: You revise until breakfast. The real exam paper is written in a normal language. You're absurdly relieved.
opt.left.say.1 [ba0aba] = 你一直复习到早餐。真正的试卷是用正常语言写的。你如释重负得有点荒唐。
# en: Go back to sleep
opt.right.label [097b30] = 接着睡
# en: You dream again. This time the goat gives you full marks. You choose to take this as an omen.
opt.right.say.1 [c9ff1e] = 你又做梦了。这次山羊给了你满分。你决定把这当作一个好兆头。

@event life_garden_plot
# en: A Patch of Earth
title [675687] = 一方泥土
# en: Old Maud is giving out the abandoned plots behind the greenhouses. There's one left: small, weedy and full of rocks. "It's yours if you want it," she says. "Gardens are a lot of work. Most of the work is noticing."
text [492379] = 老莫德正在分发温室后面那些废弃的小块地。还剩一块：小小的，杂草丛生，满是石头。“想要的话就归你，”她说，“种园子很费功夫。大部分功夫是用心去看。”
# en: A small square of freshly turned earth behind the greenhouses, a wooden stake with a student's name painted on it, a watering can beside it.
scene [ae502d] = 温室后面一小块刚翻过的泥土，插着一根写有学生名字的木桩，旁边放着一只水壶。
# en: Take the plot
opt.left.label [a249fc] = 接下这块地
# en: You spend a whole weekend clearing rocks. By spring, you have lettuces, three violent mandrakes and a strange purple flower nobody can name.
opt.left.say.1 [205e70] = 你花了整整一个周末清理石头。到了春天，你有了生菜、三棵暴躁的曼德拉草，和一朵谁也叫不出名字的奇怪紫花。
# en: Leave it for someone else
opt.right.label [43df3f] = 留给别人
# en: A shy first-year takes it and grows giant pumpkins. You feel oddly proud of them.
opt.right.say.1 [a9e348] = 一个害羞的一年级生接手了它，种出了巨大的南瓜。你莫名为它们感到骄傲。

@event life_pen_pal
# en: A Letter From Thornwick
title [64e8f7] = 荆木来信
# en: A letter arrives from a stranger at Thornwick Academy — the rival school. "Dear Lumenhold student chosen at random," it begins. "I'm told you're all insufferable. Prove me wrong?"
text [a313a2] = 一封信来自对手学校荆木学院的一个陌生人。“亲爱的、随机抽中的流明堡学生，”信的开头写道，“听说你们全都让人受不了。能证明我错了吗？”
# en: A letter with a green Thornwick seal open on a desk, beside a reply half-written in Lumenhold blue ink.
scene [72beee] = 书桌上摊开一封盖着荆木绿色封印的信，旁边是一封用流明堡蓝墨水写了一半的回信。
# en: Write back
opt.left.label [ae4ebf] = 回信
# en: Your reply is four pages long and only slightly insufferable. The answer arrives within a week. You've made a friend in enemy territory.
opt.left.say.1 [3f96bc] = 你的回信写了四页，只是稍微有点让人受不了。不到一星期回信就到了。你在敌方领土交到了一个朋友。
# en: Ignore it
opt.right.label [e2ae0c] = 不理它
# en: You ignore it. A second letter arrives: "Insufferable AND rude. Noted." You almost reply. Almost.
opt.right.say.1 [a47716] = 你没理它。第二封信来了：“让人受不了，而且没礼貌。记下了。”你差点就回信了。差一点。

@event life_three_headed_puppy
# en: A Very Lost Puppy
title [b1e6d0] = 一只迷路的小狗
# en: There is a puppy in the dormitory corridor. It has three heads. One is eating a shoe, one is licking the wall, one is howling. It is very lost and, all three heads agree, very hungry.
text [01f554] = 宿舍走廊里有一只小狗。它有三个头。一个在啃鞋，一个在舔墙，一个在嚎叫。它彻底迷路了，而且——三个头一致认为——非常饿。
# en: A puppy with three heads sitting in a corridor, one head chewing a shoe, one licking a wall, one howling mournfully.
scene [9614f5] = 一只三头小狗坐在走廊里，一个头在嚼鞋子，一个在舔墙，一个在悲伤地嚎叫。
# en: Feed it and find its owner
opt.left.label [f395df] = 喂它，然后找它的主人
# en: You follow its owner's frantic shouting to Professor Brask's office. She weeps with relief. The puppy's three heads each lick you once, in strict order.
opt.left.say.1 [29bcbc] = 你循着主人焦急的呼喊找到了布拉斯克教授的办公室。她松了一口气，哭了出来。小狗的三个头严格按顺序各舔了你一下。
# en: Call Professor Brask
opt.right.label [a54d9d] = 叫布拉斯克教授来
# en: Brask arrives at a run with a lead and three biscuits. "Bad boys," she says fondly. All three heads look deeply ashamed.
opt.right.say.1 [b589e2] = 布拉斯克拿着牵绳和三块饼干一路跑来。“坏孩子们，”她宠溺地说。三个头看起来都羞愧极了。

@event life_bell_tower
# en: The Midnight Bell
title [2cdb21] = 午夜钟声
# en: Tradition: once in your time at Lumenhold, you must ring the old bell at midnight without getting caught. Your dorm has decided tonight is your night.
text [97f4cd] = 传统：在流明堡的日子里，你必须有一次在午夜敲响古钟而不被抓到。你的宿舍认定今晚就是你的夜晚。
# en: A dark bell tower interior, ropes hanging down, a group of students at the bottom daring one of their number to climb.
scene [33ec20] = 漆黑的钟楼内部，钟绳垂落，一群学生站在底下怂恿其中一人爬上去。
# en: Climb and ring it (Guile)
opt.left.label [320427] = 爬上去敲钟（诡计）
# en: BONG. The whole castle wakes. By the time the prefects reach the tower you're back in bed, innocent and smug.
opt.left.say.1 [37e43a] = 当——整座城堡都醒了。等级长们赶到钟楼时，你已经回到床上，一脸无辜又得意。
# en: BONG — and Bram is at the bottom of the stairs when you come down. Detention. But you rang it, and everybody heard.
opt.left.say.2 [0df3f9] = 当——而你下来时，布拉姆就站在楼梯底下。禁闭。但你敲响了它，所有人都听见了。
# en: Decline the dare
opt.right.label [78dc24] = 拒绝这个挑战
# en: Someone else rings it instead and becomes a legend. You'll always wonder.
opt.right.say.1 [a936f5] = 别人替你敲响了钟，成了传奇。你会一直好奇的。

@event life_fog_maze
# en: The Fog Maze
title [a0d483] = 雾中迷宫
# en: Fog has come up off the lake so thick you can't see your own feet. The path to the greenhouses has become a maze. Somewhere ahead, someone is calling for help, faintly.
text [ee15c0] = 湖上升起的雾浓得你连自己的脚都看不见。通往温室的小路变成了一座迷宫。前方某处，有人在微弱地呼救。
# en: The academy grounds swallowed by thick white fog, hedges looming like walls, a lantern glowing faintly ahead.
scene [666c24] = 学院的庭院被浓密的白雾吞没，树篱像墙一样隐约耸立，前方一盏灯笼发着微光。
# en: Follow the voice
opt.left.label [f27ba5] = 循着声音走
# en: You find a first-year sitting on a bench, completely lost, sixty feet from the door. You walk them in. They tell everyone you saved their life.
opt.left.say.1 [2c5755] = 你找到一个坐在长椅上、彻底迷路的一年级生，离门只有六十英尺。你领着对方进去。对方逢人便说你救了自己一命。
# en: You walk in circles for an hour and end up exactly where you started. The voice was a very clever crow.
opt.left.say.2 [fc0168] = 你绕了一个钟头的圈子，最后回到了起点。那声音是一只非常聪明的乌鸦。
# en: Cast a light and wait
opt.right.label [988921] = 点亮光芒，原地等待
# en: You raise a floating light and wait. One by one, three lost students find their way to it. You feel like a lighthouse.
opt.right.say.1 [380b7f] = 你升起一团漂浮的光，静静等待。三个迷路的学生一个接一个地找到了它。你觉得自己像一座灯塔。

@event life_wishing_well
# en: The Wishing Well
title [8cab57] = 许愿井
# en: In the old cloister there's a wishing well. The inscription says: "ONE COIN, ONE WISH, ONE PRICE." The bottom glitters with three hundred years of coins.
text [0ae5ea] = 古老的回廊里有一口许愿井。铭文写着：“一枚硬币，一个愿望，一个代价。”井底闪烁着三百年来的硬币。
# en: An old stone well in the corner of a cloister, coins glinting at the bottom, a carved inscription half-worn away.
scene [9ea5b9] = 回廊角落里一口古老的石井，井底硬币闪闪发光，一段刻字已经磨损了一半。
# en: Throw in a coin and wish
opt.left.label [ce57aa] = 投一枚硬币许愿
# en: You wish for a good month. It is, mostly. Coincidence, probably.
opt.left.say.1 [4c845e] = 你许愿这个月过得顺利。大体上确实如此。大概是巧合。
# en: You wish. The well hiccups and spits your coin back out. Apparently, you can't afford that wish.
opt.left.say.2 [3fc324] = 你许了愿。井打了个嗝，把你的硬币吐了出来。看来这个愿望你付不起。
# en: Fish out a few old coins
opt.right.label [dbef4d] = 捞几枚古币出来
# en: Twelve crowns' worth of antique coins. The well is silent. Disapprovingly silent.
opt.right.say.1 [1e4d79] = 价值十二克朗的古董硬币。井沉默着。不以为然地沉默着。
# en: The well bites. You lose your own purse in it. ONE PRICE indeed.
opt.right.say.2 [708beb] = 井咬人。你把自己的钱袋掉了进去。果然是“一个代价”。

@event life_borrowed_broom
# en: The Borrowed Broom
title [c73e99] = 借来的扫帚
# en: A second-year lends you their broom for an errand. Midway across the lake, you discover why they were so keen to lend it: it is extremely ticklish, and it hates you.
text [ca31e2] = 一个二年级生把扫帚借给你去跑腿。飞到湖中央时，你才发现对方为什么那么乐意借给你：它极其怕痒，而且讨厌你。
# en: A student clinging to a bucking broom high above the castle, its bristles on fire, a smaller student on the ground waving frantically.
scene [c7a1ed] = 一名学生紧紧抓着一把在城堡上空乱蹦的扫帚，帚尾着了火，地上一个小个子学生在拼命挥手。
# en: Wrestle it home (Vigor)
opt.left.label [edf039] = 硬把它拽回去（体魄）
# en: You land in a heap on the lawn, triumphant and windswept. The broom sulks. The second-year owes you a favour.
opt.left.say.1 [90315b] = 你一头栽在草坪上，得意洋洋、头发凌乱。扫帚生着闷气。那个二年级生欠你一个人情。
# en: You land in the lake. The broom flies home without you, very pleased with itself.
opt.left.say.2 [a5f5be] = 你掉进了湖里。扫帚自己飞回了家，非常得意。
# en: Soothe it (Charm)
opt.right.label [694e2a] = 安抚它（魅力）
# en: You talk to it gently all the way across. It purrs. Brooms shouldn't purr. Now it follows you around.
opt.right.say.1 [542704] = 你一路温柔地跟它说话。它发出了呼噜声。扫帚不该会呼噜的。现在它到哪儿都跟着你。
# en: It is not soothed. It is, if anything, more ticklish.
opt.right.say.2 [1a061b] = 它没有被安抚。要说有什么变化，那就是更怕痒了。

@event life_double_trouble
# en: Your Double Is Loose
title [0b749f] = 你的分身跑了
# en: An illusion of you — one you thought you'd dismissed — is still wandering the castle. It has been to three of your classes, flirted with a prefect, and volunteered you for the choir.
text [e2deca] = 一个你以为早就解除了的分身幻象，还在城堡里到处游荡。它去上了你的三节课，和一位级长调情，还替你报名了合唱团。
# en: A student staring in horror across a crowded corridor at a perfect copy of themselves, cheerfully chatting up a professor.
scene [f7b09f] = 一名学生惊恐地隔着拥挤的走廊望着一个和自己一模一样的复制品，那复制品正兴高采烈地和一位教授攀谈。
# en: Catch it (Guile)
opt.left.label [c3ddc2] = 抓住它（诡计）
# en: You corner it in a broom cupboard. It looks at you, shrugs and pops like a bubble. The prefect, however, still expects a date.
opt.left.say.1 [75bb7a] = 你把它堵在扫帚间里。它看着你，耸了耸肩，像泡泡一样“啪”地消失了。不过，那位级长仍然在等着约会。
# en: It escapes, and spends a week as the most charming version of you. People are disappointed when you come back.
opt.left.say.2 [4bfacb] = 它溜走了，当了一个星期最有魅力的你。你回来的时候，大家都有点失望。
# en: Let it run its course
opt.right.label [0407c9] = 随它去吧
# en: It attends your lectures and takes better notes than you do. When it fades after a week, you're almost sorry.
opt.right.say.1 [c344b5] = 它替你上课，笔记记得比你还好。一星期后它消散时，你几乎有点舍不得。

@event life_auction
# en: The Lost-Property Auction
title [a95e5d] = 失物拍卖会
# en: Once a year the caretaker auctions off unclaimed lost property. There's a box nobody wants that hums faintly. The bidding starts at two crowns. Nobody's bidding.
text [29b120] = 每年一次，管理员会拍卖无人认领的失物。有一个没人要的盒子在微微嗡鸣。起拍价两克朗。没人出价。
# en: A crowded hall, a caretaker with a gavel at a lectern, tables piled with lost scarves, wands, boots and one suspiciously humming box.
scene [c3957c] = 拥挤的大厅，管理员手持木槌站在讲台后，桌上堆满了丢失的围巾、魔杖、靴子，还有一个可疑地嗡嗡作响的盒子。
# en: Bid on the humming box
opt.left.label [fb0360] = 竞拍那个嗡鸣的盒子
# en: Inside: a music box that plays a different song every time you open it. Each one makes you think of something new.
opt.left.say.1 [2acaf5] = 里面是一个音乐盒，每次打开都会放一首不同的曲子。每一首都让你想到新的东西。
# en: Inside: a very old, very annoyed hiccup curse, which immediately transfers itself to you.
opt.left.say.2 [04b453] = 里面是一个非常古老、非常恼火的打嗝诅咒，它立刻转移到了你身上。
# en: Buy a good warm scarf instead
opt.right.label [98578d] = 改买一条暖和的好围巾
# en: A scarf of real Northern wool, slightly singed. It's the warmest thing you've ever owned.
opt.right.say.1 [e163d0] = 一条真正的北境羊毛围巾，有点烧焦。这是你拥有过的最暖和的东西。

@event life_village_busking
# en: Busking in the Village
title [2797e6] = 小镇卖艺
# en: You're short on crowns, and the village square has a fountain, an empty hat and a crowd of shoppers. You do know a few songs.
text [f6178e] = 你手头缺克朗，而小镇广场上有一座喷泉、一顶空帽子和一群购物的人。你确实会几首歌。
# en: A cobbled village square, a student singing beside a fountain with an upturned hat at their feet, villagers pausing to listen.
scene [96e354] = 铺着鹅卵石的小镇广场，一名学生在喷泉边唱歌，脚边放着一顶翻过来的帽子，镇民们驻足聆听。
# en: Sing your heart out
opt.left.label [ebf8e1] = 尽情放声歌唱
# en: A small crowd gathers. Someone requests an encore. The hat fills with copper and one silver coin from a weeping old man.
opt.left.say.1 [f60a68] = 一小群人围了过来。有人要求返场。帽子里装满了铜币，还有一位泪流满面的老人投下的一枚银币。
# en: Two crowns and a sympathetic look from a dog. Busking is harder than it looks.
opt.left.say.2 [e49aa9] = 两克朗，外加一条狗同情的眼神。卖艺比看起来难多了。
# en: Play the street-magic act instead (Arcana)
opt.right.label [d8a6f0] = 改演街头魔术（奥术）
# en: You make doves out of the fountain spray. Children scream with joy. The hat overflows.
opt.right.say.1 [747727] = 你用喷泉的水雾变出鸽子。孩子们开心得尖叫。帽子都装不下了。
# en: Your doves come out as damp sparrows. People are kind about it.
opt.right.say.2 [def817] = 你变出来的鸽子成了湿漉漉的麻雀。大家都很包容。

@event life_moths
# en: A Storm of Moths
title [34c527] = 飞蛾风暴
# en: You open your door to find your room full of moths — thousands of them, pale as moonlight, circling your candle in silent spirals. It's eerie. It's also, you can't help noticing, beautiful.
text [b3079c] = 你推开门，发现房间里满是飞蛾——成千上万只，白得像月光，绕着你的蜡烛无声地盘旋。很诡异。你也不得不承认，很美。
# en: A dormitory room filled with thousands of pale moths circling a single candle, a student standing in the doorway, astonished.
scene [ba25b5] = 宿舍房间里成千上万只苍白的飞蛾绕着一支蜡烛盘旋，一名学生站在门口，惊呆了。
# en: Open the window and let them go
opt.left.label [09f522] = 打开窗放它们走
# en: They pour out into the night in a silver river. One stays behind, on your pillow, for a week. You name it Gregory.
opt.left.say.1 [582ae8] = 它们像一条银色的河流涌入夜色。有一只留了下来，在你的枕头上待了一个星期。你给它起名叫格雷戈里。
# en: Study them
opt.right.label [3a81ec] = 研究它们
# en: They're luna moths, migrating — and drawn to something in your room. You find it: a crumb of moonpetal on your sleeve. Mystery solved. Mostly.
opt.right.say.1 [eb5366] = 它们是迁徙中的月形天蚕蛾——被你房间里的什么东西吸引了过来。你找到了：袖子上一点月瓣花的碎屑。谜团解开了。大体上。
